From 8d5a0914469d94cc4b921851143ade03bc6c6bb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:45:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 38/47] workflows: build galago as locked on push, and with
 updated inputs daily

The galago build ran `nix flake update` every hour and threw the new
flake.lock away, so it never built the configuration as committed, and
no run left a lock to take.  It has failed on every run since October
31, each time on a change in the latest inputs: nixpkgs refused to
evaluate gtk+ 2 and then dropped brave-origin, the bcachefs module did
not build against Linux 7.4-rc1 to rc3 of linuxPackages_testing,
emacs-git from the unpinned overlay failed on a patch that upstream had
applied, and from November 23 the kernel failed on the xhci patch then
in commons.nix, which Linux 7.4-rc4 contains.  Since cache.nixos.org
does not have nixpkgs master yet, the runs also built Electron and the
kernel from source for hours, and some hit the limit of six hours.

Build flake.lock as committed on each push to master instead, and
update the inputs only once a day, or when dispatched with `update`.
That run lists the updated inputs in its summary and keeps its
flake.lock as an artifact, so that a lock which built, and whose paths
are in Cachix, can be committed deliberately; the run itself never
commits it.  A dry run of galago with the committed lock lists a few
dozen derivations to build, such as emacs-git and the bcachefs module,
and fetches the rest.

The new upload step pins its action to a commit, as check.yml does.
---
 .github/workflows/build-galago.yml | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build-galago.yml b/.github/workflows/build-galago.yml
index eb466f5..3732b0a 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build-galago.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build-galago.yml
@@ -1,8 +1,38 @@
+# Builds galago and pushes each path it builds to the yzhou216 Cachix
+# cache.
+#
+# On a push to master, it builds the inputs that flake.lock pins, which
+# is what `nixos-rebuild switch --flake .` deploys, so a failure there
+# means that the committed configuration does not build.
+#
+# Once a day, and when dispatched with `update`, it runs
+# `nix flake update` first, to find out whether galago builds with the
+# latest inputs and to fill the cache before the next update.  A
+# failure there is breakage upstream that updating would bring in.  The
+# job summary lists the inputs that changed, and the run keeps the
+# updated flake.lock as an artifact; to commit the inputs that the run
+# built, fetch it with
+# `gh run download <run> -R yzhou216/flake -n flake.lock`.
+name: build galago
 on:
+  push:
+    branches: [master]
   schedule:
-    - cron: "0 */1 * * *"
+    - cron: "17 3 * * *"
   workflow_dispatch:
-
+    inputs:
+      update:
+        description: Update the flake inputs before building
+        type: boolean
+        default: true
+permissions:
+  contents: read
+# Explicit shell adds -o pipefail, which `nix flake update | tee` needs
+defaults:
+  run:
+    shell: bash
+env:
+  UPDATE: ${{ github.event_name == 'schedule' || inputs.update }}
 jobs:
   build:
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
@@ -18,7 +48,14 @@ jobs:
           name: yzhou216
           authToken: ${{ secrets.CACHIX_AUTH_TOKEN }}
       - name: Update flake.lock
-        run: nix flake update
+        if: env.UPDATE == 'true'
+        run: |
+          nix flake update 2>&1 | tee update.log
+          {
+            echo '```'
+            cat update.log
+            echo '```'
+          } >>"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
 
       # Same target as `nixos-rebuild switch --flake .`;
       # `--keep-going` builds the rest if one package fails, and
@@ -29,3 +66,9 @@ jobs:
             --keep-going \
             --no-link \
             ".#nixosConfigurations.galago.config.system.build.toplevel"
+
+      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@cf430e030ddbb5b0abf93d22962f4752f3646cd9 # v7.0.2
+        if: always() && env.UPDATE == 'true'
+        with:
+          name: flake.lock
+          path: flake.lock
-- 
